    <h2>The calls we get every week</h2>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>A breaker that will not stay on</strong>, or trips whenever two things run at once.</li>
        <li><strong>Outlets or a whole room with no power</strong>, often a tripped GFCI somewhere else in the house.</li>
        <li><strong>Lights that flicker or dim</strong> when the furnace, the AC or the dryer starts.</li>
        <li><strong>Warm outlet covers, buzzing switches or a faint burning smell</strong>, which should never wait.</li>
    </ul>
    <h2>How we troubleshoot</h2>
    <p>We start with questions: when it happens, what else is running, what changed recently. Then we test the circuit from the panel outward rather than replacing parts and hoping. You get an explanation of what failed and why, and a fixed price for the repair.</p>
    <p>If the fault is a sign of something bigger, such as an undersized panel or brittle old wiring, we will say so and put it in writing, with no pressure to do it today.</p>
    <h2>When to call right away</h2>
    <p>A burning smell, scorch marks, sparking, or an outlet too hot to touch: switch off that circuit at the panel and <a href="/emergency/">call our 24/7 line</a>.</p>
